message: "If you use BDR v1.2.0-rc2, please cite this software release and the associated scientific preprint where appropriate."
title: "Banco de Dados Resolutivo (BDR) / Resolutive Database Engine"
version: "1.2.0-rc2"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Matos"
    given-names: "Marcelo Roldão"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-6075-4680"
repository-code: "https://github.com/marceloroldao/resolutive-DB"
url: "https://github.com/marceloroldao/resolutive-DB/releases/tag/v1.2.0-rc2"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22821283"
abstract: >-
  BDR v1.2.0-rc2 is a published pre-release candidate in the v1.2 line. It
  preserves the v1.1 atomic BDW4 persistence model while validating the Atomic
  C ABI v2 and Memoria.ia integration contract. Multi-operation
  PerOperationSync batches remain one logical batch, one sequence and one
  all-or-nothing recovery boundary. Native WAL torn-tail recovery, durability,
  cold restart and end-to-end Memoria.ia recovery gates passed for this
  candidate. Performance claims remain workload-specific.
keywords:
  - resolutive database
  - BDR
  - Memoria.ia
  - atomic batch
  - BDW4
  - key-value database
  - persistent storage
  - write-ahead log
  - crash recovery
  - C++ API
  - C ABI
  - reproducible research
